  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 144 AM MST Wed Nov 25 2026\n\nForecast remains mainly unchanged. Dry weather is still likely \ninto Thursday. The flow turns northwesterly which favors the \ncentral mountains around Stanley and the upper Snake highlands. \nQPF totals for these areas are 0.25 to 0.50 inches into Saturday\nmorning. Most snow will fall above 6000 feet. Snow amounts are \nonly expected to be a few inches in these areas. There is a \nslightly stronger push of moisture that arrives Friday night \ninto Saturday which may spread precipitation into the southern \nand southeast highlands. However, qpf amounts look light, \nperhaps up to 0.25 inches in those areas. We should see a break \nuntil Sunday Night into Monday when a trough of low pressure \npasses through from the west. This may result in better chances \nfor widespread precipitation.",
